From: mi5-droidspaces-kernel <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] xt_qtaguid: keep live iface stats, but only for init_net devices

Droidspaces' non-GKI patch set removes the dev_get_stats() call from
/proc/net/xt_qtaguid/iface_stat_fmt entirely, because reading statistics of a
network device that lives in a container network namespace can dereference a
netdev that is being torn down by that namespace.

Dropping the call also drops the live rx/tx counters of every phone interface,
which is a regression the stock ROM does not have (netd reads this file for
per-interface statistics on Android 8).

Instead, only call dev_get_stats() for devices that are still in init_net.  All
interfaces the phone creates itself are init_net devices, so their output is
unchanged; devices moved into a container namespace report zeros, exactly like
inactive interfaces did before.

Signed-off-by: mi5-droidspaces-kernel <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 net/netfilter/xt_qtaguid.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/netfilter/xt_qtaguid.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/xt_qtaguid.c
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <linux/skbuff.h>
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 #include <net/addrconf.h>
+#include <net/net_namespace.h>
 #include <net/sock.h>
 #include <net/tcp.h>
 #include <net/udp.h>
@@ -748,7 +749,8 @@
 
 	iface_entry = list_entry(v, struct iface_stat, list);
 
-	if (iface_entry->active) {
+	if (iface_entry->active &&
+	    net_eq(dev_net(iface_entry->net_dev), &init_net)) {
 		stats = dev_get_stats(iface_entry->net_dev,
 				      &dev_stats);
 	} else {
